@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+.\" Vibe coded by Codex
+.Dd October 25, 2026
+.Dt ANSILOVE_TEXT 3
+.Os
+.Sh NAME
+.Nm ansilove_text
+.Nd extract the final character layout as printable ASCII
+.Sh SYNOPSIS
+.In ansilove.h
+.Ft int
+.Fo ansilove_text
+.Fa "struct ansilove_ctx *ctx"
+.Fa "const struct ansilove_options *options"
+.Fa "int (*loader)(struct ansilove_ctx *, struct ansilove_options *)"
+.Fa "char **buffer"
+.Fa "size_t *length"
+.Fc
+.Sh DESCRIPTION
+The
+.Nm
+function runs one of the seven standard format loaders with an ASCII output
+backend, without generating a PNG or allocating a full pixel image.
+The caller must load the input and remove metadata from
+.Va ctx->length
+as for normal image rendering.
+The loader must be one of
+.Fn ansilove_ansi ,
+.Fn ansilove_artworx ,
+.Fn ansilove_binary ,
+.Fn ansilove_icedraw ,
+.Fn ansilove_pcboard ,
+.Fn ansilove_tundra ,
+or
+.Fn ansilove_xbin .
+.Pp
+On success,
+.Fa buffer
+receives an allocated, NUL-terminated string and
+.Fa length
+receives its size excluding the NUL.
+The caller must release the string with
+.Fn free .
+Caller options and existing PNG data are preserved.
+Output consists only of bytes 32 through 126 and line feeds.
+Other glyphs and characters whose foreground equals their background become
+spaces, preserving cell positions and overwrites.
+Trailing spaces and outer blank rows are removed.
+An entirely blank screen produces an empty string.
+The character grid is limited to 64 MiB.
+.Pp
+This is the final image's character layout, not an animation transcript or OCR.
+Cleared and overwritten text is absent. Custom fonts may remap ASCII glyphs.
+Existing loader semantics, including ANSI cursor and erasure behavior, apply.
+.Sh RETURN VALUES
+Returns 0 on success or -1 on failure, setting
+.Va ctx->error .
+On failure, valid output pointers are set to NULL and zero.
+.Sh SEE ALSO
+.Xr ansilove_ansi 3 ,
+.Xr ansilove_error 3
